#### Creating new documents inside a batch

`executeBatch` only applies actions; it does not create the target documents for you. To create a document in a batch job, build the document in memory and emit the CREATE_DOCUMENT + UPGRADE_DOCUMENT pair with the `createDocumentAction` and `upgradeDocumentAction` helpers exported from `@powerhousedao/reactor`. Both are document-scope actions, so the job plan must use `scope: "document"`.

```typescript
import { createDocumentAction, upgradeDocumentAction } from "@powerhousedao/reactor";
import { documentModelCreateDocument, normalizeDocumentModelVersion } from "document-model";

const doc = documentModelCreateDocument();

const actions = [
  createDocumentAction({
    model: doc.header.documentType,
    version: 0,
    documentId: doc.header.id,
    signing: {
      signature: doc.header.id,
      publicKey: doc.header.sig.publicKey,
      nonce: doc.header.sig.nonce,
      createdAtUtcIso: doc.header.createdAtUtcIso,
      documentType: doc.header.documentType,
    },
    name: doc.header.name,
    branch: doc.header.branch,
    meta: doc.header.meta,
    protocolVersions: doc.header.protocolVersions ?? { "base-reducer": 2 },
  }),
  upgradeDocumentAction({
    documentId: doc.header.id,
    model: doc.header.documentType,
    fromVersion: 0,
    toVersion: normalizeDocumentModelVersion(doc.state.document?.version),
    initialState: doc.state,
  }),
];

// then: { key: "budget", documentId: doc.header.id, scope: "document", branch: "main", actions, dependsOn: [] }
```

### Built-in document models

Two document models ship with the platform and must be registered explicitly on any reactor that stores drives or document models:

```typescript
import { ReactorBuilder } from "@powerhousedao/reactor";
import { documentModelDocumentModelModule, documentModelCreateDocument } from "document-model";
import { driveDocumentModelModule, driveCreateDocument, addFile } from "@powerhousedao/shared/document-drive";

const reactor = await new ReactorBuilder()
  .withDocumentModelSources([documentModelDocumentModelModule, driveDocumentModelModule])
  .build();

// IReactor has no `drives` helper (that lives on IReactorClient): build the drive
// document yourself and submit it with `create`.
const drive = driveCreateDocument({ global: { name: "My drive", icon: null, nodes: [] } });
const job = await reactor.create(drive);
```

`driveDocumentModelModule`, `driveCreateDocument`, and the drive action creators (`addFile`, `addFolder`, `moveNode`, …) come from `@powerhousedao/shared/document-drive`. `documentModelDocumentModelModule` and `documentModelCreateDocument` come from `document-model`.

### Creating a document from actions

`IReactor.execute` and `executeBatch` take actions, not documents, so a new document is created by issuing the two genesis actions yourself. Both creators are exported from `@powerhousedao/reactor`:

```typescript
import { createDocumentAction, upgradeDocumentAction } from "@powerhousedao/reactor";
import { documentModelCreateState } from "document-model";

const documentId = crypto.randomUUID();
const actions = [
  // CREATE_DOCUMENT — `model` is the document type, `version` is always 0
  createDocumentAction({ model: "powerhouse/document-model", version: 0, documentId }),
  // UPGRADE_DOCUMENT 0 -> 1 — seeds the initial state
  upgradeDocumentAction({
    model: "powerhouse/document-model",
    fromVersion: 0,
    toVersion: 1,
    documentId,
    initialState: documentModelCreateState(),
  }),
];
```

Both actions are `document`-scope, so a job plan carrying them must declare `scope: "document"`. `createDocumentAction` also accepts optional `slug`, `name`, `branch`, `meta` and `protocolVersions`.

### Built-in document models and drive helpers

Two document models ship with the platform and must be registered explicitly if you want to use them:

```typescript
import { documentModelDocumentModelModule, documentModelCreateState } from "document-model";
import {
  driveDocumentModelModule,
  driveCreateDocument,
  driveDocumentType, // "powerhouse/document-drive"
  addFile,
} from "@powerhousedao/shared/document-drive";

const { reactor, eventBus } = await new ReactorBuilder()
